  <p class="bk-label bk-tight">For founders + select founder-like executives</p>
  <p>Welcome to <strong>FOUNDRland</strong>.</p>

  <p class="bk-label bk-tight">What we’ll do in your sprints:</p>
  <p>
    Each sprint is 60 minutes and stays fluid based on what’s most relevant in the moment. The flow follows a
    consistent arc:
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>1) Clarity:</strong> We start by analyzing the issue and making sure you see where you’re holding a story as
    if it’s reality. The goal is to restore the core lever: you’re in control of how you emotionally respond to a
    situation — and you can choose differently.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>2) Decision:</strong> Once the issue is clear, we build the map moving forward. Then we re-route the issue
    from “problem” to opportunity: What is the distinction you need? The output here is a clean decision and the next
    step.
  </p>
  <p><strong>3) Execution:</strong> We move from insight into your system:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Integration through reflections to ground insights into the physical/neurological nervous system</li>
    <li>Habit rerouting: we work with thought patterns / self-talk → emotional responses → actions</li>
    <li>
      We look at patterns on a 7‑day week basis and practice the new responses — to create psychological safety in the
      new decisions and habits.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>Most clients feel lighter, regain clarity, and can take new empowered actions from that frame.</p>

  <p class="bk-label bk-tight">How to prepare for each sprint: (Copy/paste and answer these in a note)</p>
  <ol>
    <li>What’s the one thing that’s most “alive” right now?</li>
    <li>What decision are you avoiding or second‑guessing?</li>
    <li>What keeps breaking down after you “know what to do”?</li>
    <li>What’s the typical chain of behaviors (from self‑talk → emotion → action)?</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Bring that note into the session.</p>
